# .git-blame-ignore-revs
#
# Bulk stylistic/housekeeping commits that touched many files without making
# meaningful content changes. Listed here so `git blame` (locally and on GitHub)
# skips these revisions and shows the last *meaningful* change to each line.
#
# Also consumed by tools/doc_audit/audit.py to improve staleness scoring.
#
# To activate for local blame:
#   git config blame.ignoreRevsFile .git-blame-ignore-revs
#
# Format: one full commit SHA per line, preceded by a comment explaining it.

